     mmppiipp — MPLS IP layer 2 pseudowire

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ppsseeuuddoo--ddeevviiccee mmppiipp

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The mmppiipp interface is used to create an MPLS IP layer 2 tunnel between
     two points.

     An mmppiipp interface can be created at runtime using the iiffccoonnffiigg mmppiipp_N
     ccrreeaattee command, or by setting up a hostname.if(5) configuration file for
     netstart(8).  The interface itself can be configured with ifconfig(8).

     The local MPLS label, the remote MPLS label and neighbor, use of pseu‐
     dowire control words, or flow-aware transport are normally configured af‐
     ter negotiation with a remote system using ldpd(8), but it is also possi‐
     ble to configure them manually using ifconfig(8).

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     Create a pseudowire with local label 20 and remote label 21 on neighbor
     10.254.0.1:

           # ifconfig mpip5 create
           # ifconfig mpip5 mplslabel 20 pweneighbor 21 10.254.0.1
           # ifconfig mpip5 up

     Disable the use of the Pseudowire Emulation Edge-to-Edge (PWE3) Control
     Word, and enable the use of a Flow label for Flow-Aware Transport of
     Pseudowires:

           # ifconfig mpip5 -pwecw pwefat

